  "en": {
    "messages": [
      {
        "id": "m_a1",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Magic in this world should be equivalent exchange: to gain something you pay an equal price.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "m_a2",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Then let the price be memory loss: the stronger the spell, the more precious a memory the caster forgets.",
        "insertedToEditor": true,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "m_a3",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Fantasy with magic is such a rich theme. There are so many great works across history.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "m_a4",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Memory as the price, I like it. Let's say lost memories never come back.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "m_b1",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The protagonist Selena grew up in an orphanage and never knew her parents.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "m_b2",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "What if the mentor Gaius discovered her magical talent at the orphanage and took her in?",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "m_b3",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Gaius is strict but kind at heart, a father figure to Selena.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "m_b4",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Nice. Once the family setup is fixed the character gains a real backbone.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "m_c1",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The capital has three tiers: the lower artisan quarter, the middle merchant district, the upper noble quarter.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "m_c2",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Make the Silver Gate between the upper and middle tiers a checkpoint, so class-based movement limits drive the plot.",
        "insertedToEditor": true,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "m_d1",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The antagonist Valca is driven by revenge; he lost his whole family to a magic accident.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "m_d2",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "A revenge motive is a solid classic, and readers empathize with it easily.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "m_e1",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "I want to open the story with a rain scene, Selena arriving at the capital.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "m_e2",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Rain can double as a 'washing away memory' motif, echoing the price of magic.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "m_x1",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Lovely weather today. I went for a short walk.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "m_x2",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Breaks matter. Hope the writing goes well afterwards.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_0",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Let's lock in the magic system. The Tideweave lets casters borrow strength from ocean currents, but only within 300 paces of saltwater.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_1",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Good constraint. I'd add that each Tideweave casting drains the user's body heat, so casters shiver violently after big spells and need wool cloaks even in summer.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_2",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Yes, and the heat-drain is cumulative — three castings in an hour can drop a caster into deadly hypothermia.",
        "insertedToEditor": true,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_3",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Nice, that works well.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_4",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Backstory for Captain Veyla Orn: she lost her left hand at the Siege of Karrowmoor when she was nineteen, defending the granary gate.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_5",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "We could give her a brass prosthetic forged by the smith Dolian, who carved tiny gull motifs into the knuckles as a private joke about her seasickness.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_6",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "That's a strong detail.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_7",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "She still has phantom pain in the missing hand whenever a storm approaches — it became her crew's weather forecast.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_8",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The city of Brannock is built in five concentric rings, with the bronze Foundry Ring at the center and the slum Mudring on the outermost edge.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_9",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Travel between rings goes through the Sluice Gates, which only open at dawn and dusk — so being caught in the wrong ring at night means you're stuck there.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_10",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Love that layout.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_11",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The Foundry Ring's heat keeps the whole city warm, so the closer you live to the center, the higher your status.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_12",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The Ashen Concord faction wants to extinguish every dragon-flame in the realm because they believe fire-magic is what cracked the old moon.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_13",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Their agents carry frostglass vials that smother flames instantly, and they brand themselves with a snuffed-candle sigil over the heart.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_14",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Great, that's coherent.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_15",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Their leader, Mother Quench, was herself burned as a child in the Pyre of Saint Allow.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_16",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Timeline: the Sundering happened in the year 412, when the twin suns first appeared in the sky over Eldermarsh.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_17",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "So the novel's present should be 412 plus roughly sixty years — call it 470 — when the last people who remember a single sun are dying off.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_18",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Sounds right.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_19",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "And the Long Drought of 438 nearly emptied Eldermarsh — that's why the marsh tribes scattered.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_20",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The artifact is the Hollow Lantern: it gives light that casts no shadows, and anyone standing in its glow cannot lie.",
        "insertedToEditor": true,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_21",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "We should make its fuel rare — it burns only powdered nightbloom petals, and one petal lasts a single hour.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_22",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Perfect.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_23",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "And prolonged exposure to its light slowly bleaches the holder's eyes to milky white.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_24",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Let's design the creature called the Mirewight — a bog-dwelling thing that wears the drowned as a disguise.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_25",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "It hunts by mimicking the voice of a victim's dead loved one, luring travelers off the safe causeway into the sucking peat.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_26",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Chilling — that fits.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_27",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "You can spot a Mirewight because it casts no reflection in still water, only ripples.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_28",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Political conflict: the Salt Barons of Hesp control all the realm's salt mines and have just doubled the tithe, starving the inland duchies.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_29",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Duke Arven of Caldmere could respond by funding pirates to raid the salt galleons, sparking an undeclared sea war.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_30",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Good escalation.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_31",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The Barons retaliate by salting the duchy's wells, which is a war crime under the Pact of Hesp.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_32",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Religion detail: the Threnody Order worships silence and forbids its monks from speaking after their fortieth birthday.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_33",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "They communicate through a finger-tapping language called Knuckle-Cant, and the eldest monks are revered as 'the Truly Quiet.'",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_34",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Beautiful idea.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_35",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Their monastery, Greypsalm, is carved into a cliff so the wind never reaches it — total stillness.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_36",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Protagonist Jora's arc: she starts as a forger of trade seals in the port of Wend before she's blackmailed into the Crown's spy service.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_37",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Her forging skill becomes her spy specialty — she can replicate any noble's wax sigil from a single glance.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_38",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Yes, that ties together nicely.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_39",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The man who blackmails her is Spymaster Olwin, who holds proof she forged a dead duke's will.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_40",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The Glasswind Pass is the only mountain route into the northern kingdom, and it's blocked by ice for nine months a year.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_41",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "During the brief thaw, caravans race through, but the pass narrows at the Needle, where only one cart can fit at a time — a perfect ambush point.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_42",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Strong setpiece.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_43",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Toll-keepers at the Needle charge in fresh fruit, since nothing grows in the northern kingdom.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_44",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The royal succession runs through the maternal line: the Moonstone Crown only passes to a queen's eldest daughter, never a son.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_45",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "So Prince Halric, having no sisters, is locked out — which gives him a desperate motive to fake a daughter, perhaps an adopted heir.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_46",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "That's a juicy complication.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_47",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "If no daughter exists, the crown reverts to the Conclave of Widows, who haven't governed in three centuries.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_48",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The Emberfair is a festival held every seven years in Tellsgrove where debts are forgiven and masks are worn to hide identity.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_49",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "We can stage the assassination during the Emberfair — anonymity means the killer blends into thousands of masked dancers.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_50",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Excellent setting for it.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_51",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Tradition says you must burn last year's mask in the central bonfire, so masks are never reused — useful for the plot.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_52",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The horse breed in the story is the Dunmane, bred by the steppe Khelai to run for two days without water.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_53",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Their distinctive trait is a grey stripe down the spine, and the Khelai believe a Dunmane chooses its rider, not the reverse.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_54",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Lovely worldbuilding.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_55",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Selling a Dunmane outside the Khelai is punishable by the loss of a hand under steppe law.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_56",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The poison central to act two is Widow's Lace — odorless, brewed from a white moth's wings, and only fatal when mixed with wine.",
        "insertedToEditor": true,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_57",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "The antidote is goat's milk taken within an hour, which makes the timing of the poisoning a tense plot clock.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_58",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Great tension device.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_59",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Symptoms start as harmless laughter, so the victim seems merely drunk before collapsing.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_60",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Language detail: the Vorn people have no word for 'goodbye' — they say 'unfinished' instead, implying every parting is temporary.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_61",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "We could pay this off emotionally when a Vorn character refuses to say 'unfinished' over a grave, signaling he believes that death really is final.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_62",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "That lands well.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_63",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The Vorn also count years backward from a person's death, which they can't know — so all Vorn dates are guesses.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_64",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The wizard tower Spindlereach has rooms that rearrange themselves every midnight, so no map of the interior stays accurate.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_65",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "The library is the one fixed room — apprentices learn to navigate by always heading toward the smell of old parchment.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_66",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Clever anchor.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_67",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The tower's master, Archon Pell, is the only one who can command the rooms to hold still, and only for an hour at a time.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_68",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "The currency of the merchant republic is the Tallow Mark — coins made of pressed beeswax stamped with a queen-bee seal.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_69",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Because wax melts, the wealthy keep their fortunes in cool cellars, and a heatwave can literally bankrupt a family overnight.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_70",
        "role": "assistant",
        "text": "Wonderfully strange economy.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "g_en_71",
        "role": "user",
        "text": "Counterfeiters use paraffin instead of beeswax, detectable only by a slightly sweeter smell.",
        "insertedToEditor": false,
        "extractedCount": 0
      }
